[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read report by report, it
holds three problems. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October with two of them settled.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

| problem | since #4471 closed | issue |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` | [#1](https://github.com/szwedol/mega.dev-se01e03/issues/1) closed |
| `hint` | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired | [#2](https://github.com/szwedol/mega.dev-se01e03/issues/2) closed, not planned |
| `one-day move` | not in the engineering update | [#3](https://github.com/szwedol/mega.dev-se01e03/issues/3) **open** |

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but one problem in it is not. Dates that move by one day across time zones were
never part of the parser fix. Reports like these still belong to #3, not to #4471.
</Callout>

## The problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant in #4471 writes the day
first, so day and month swap: a 7 April reminder goes out on 4 July. This is what #4471 says it is.
[Issue #1](https://github.com/szwedol/mega.dev-se01e03/issues/1).

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form asks for the wrong order.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its
date field and reads what people type day first. People do what the hint says, and the booking
swaps. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants. The cause table on #4471 already shows this group
as "no ticket of its own"; fixing the parser does not touch it.
[Issue #2](https://github.com/szwedol/mega.dev-se01e03/issues/2).

**`one-day move`: dates shift by one day across time zones.** No swap: Lisbon gets Tuesday,
Toronto gets Monday, for the same meeting. The desk noted these reports as a one-day move and then
filed them under `parser` by tenant. They are listed in `desk-notes.json`.
[Issue #3](https://github.com/szwedol/mega.dev-se01e03/issues/3).

## How the reports were counted

- The export comes in overlapping pages, so some reports appear twice. Each id counts once.
- `causeOf()` in `causes.ts` places a report by its tenant's locale and form, not by intake's tag.
  Intake tags from the reporter's browser; it disagrees with the tenant in both directions.
- Counted the desk's way, as exported: reports in `desk-notes.json` → `oneDayMove` stay counted
  under `parser`, where their tenant files them, and get their own row and issue as well.

## Why it merged as one

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. All three problems
produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so subject matching cannot
tell them apart. Its consequences only foresee the opposite case, one bug split across subjects.
A new decision record should replace it; 0001 stays as accepted.

